{{Quote|I know what you're gonna say. I changed my hair.''"<br />"''It's nice that way.|Leia Organa and Luke Skywalker|<ref name="Episode 8">{{Film|VIII}}</ref>}}
[[File:Tarfful_and_Chewie-SWE.png|thumb|right|250px|Wookiees were covered in wooly hair from head to toe.]]
'''Hair''' was a collection of [[Color|pigmented]] thread-like strands growing from the skin of certain [[species]]. When grown on the face, it was known as a '''beard''', and the hair that formed a thick coat on some species' bodies was known as '''fur'''.

==Description==
===Biology===
[[Species]] with hair included [[human]]s,<ref name="DT">{{TCW|Death Trap}}</ref> [[Weequay]]s,<ref name="dbWEE">{{Databank|weequay|Weequay}}</ref> and many others. The thick coat of hair of certain life-forms was also referred to as fur. Such species included the [[Wookiee]]s of [[Kashyyyk]]<ref name="TRB">''[[The Rebellion Begins]]''</ref> and the [[Talz]] of [[Orto Plutonia]].<ref name="Talz">{{SWE|groups|talz|Talz}}</ref> Human males had a tendency to grow hair on their faces called a beard, or stubble when short. [[Beard suppressant]] was a substance that could prevent a beard from growing.<ref name="Lost Stars2">''[[Lost Stars]]''</ref> Hair came in a great variety of colors, lengths, and thicknesses.<ref name="TPM">{{Film|I}}</ref> As exemplified by the case of the human [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], hair lost its hue with old age.<ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref><ref name="Episode IV">{{Film|IV}}</ref> In humans, gray hairs were an easily identifiable sign of aging.<ref name="Last Shot">''[[Last Shot]]''</ref> Premature graying could also be a sign of stress, and was common in members of the [[Resistance]].<ref name="Complete Visual New">''[[Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary, New Edition]]''</ref>

===Hairstyles===
====Overview====
[[File:Sabine_Wren-Rebels_Season_3-Disney_XD_UK.png|thumb|left|250px|Sabine Wren (pictured) dyed her hair and tried to keep it short so as to keep it from getting sweaty under her helmet.]]
Hair could be styled in a vast number of ways for practical or aesthetic reasons. The human weapon experts [[Sabine Wren]] used to keep her hair short because it would often get sweaty under [[Sabine Wren's armor|her Mandalorian]] [[helmet]]. Nonetheless, she also did [[Hair dye|dye]] jobs to artificially add various colors her hair.<ref name="SRS">''[[Sabine My Rebel Sketchbook]]''</ref> Besides conventional dyes such as the purple substance extracted from the [[Carnivorous plant|carnivorous]] [[Morogian snap plant]],<ref name="Age of Resistance">{{StoryCite|story=The Bridge|book=Age of Resistance Special 1}}</ref> there existed a [[Mon Cal microplankton]] that would bond with each strand of hair, giving it a [[Bioluminescence|bioluminescent]] glow.<ref name="SRS" /> The [[Monarch of Naboo|queens]] of [[Naboo]] often sported very intricate hairstyles.<ref name="TPM" /><ref name="Episode II">{{Film|II}}</ref> A product known as [[hair gel]] could be applied to tame any unruly hairs one may have.<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref>

A [[thermal blower]] was used to dry one's hair.<ref name="SWGS">[[Star Wars: Galactic Starcruiser|''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser]]</ref> Hairstyles were sometimes influenced by trends. Many of the women at the [[Resistance base (Ajan Kloss)|Resistance base]] on [[Ajan Kloss]] were influenced by [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia's]] [[Alderaan]]ian hairstyle and wrapped their hair around their head like a crown, although [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]] believed that Leia didn't notice that she had started a trend.<ref name="TROS EE">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: Expanded Edition]]''</ref>

In the aftermath of the [[Duel on Cloud City]], [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] became obsessed with locating his son [[Luke Skywalker]]; however, instead of his son, he found [[Unidentified Luke Skywalker impostor|impostors]] who had grown their hair to match Skywalker's — medium length, layered, and blond in color — and even adopted an [[Ardee|astromech droid]] partner to make easy [[Currency|money]].<ref name="Family at War">''[[Skywalker: A Family at War]]''</ref>

====Appearance standards====
Militaries typically had requirements regarding the hairstyle of their [[officer]]s. For example, close-cropped hair was a requirement in the [[Galactic Republic]]'s [[Republic Military|military]].<ref name="ROUVG">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''</ref> In the [[Galactic Empire]], [[Imperial officer|officers]] often cut their hair short for optimal efficiency, but were allowed to keep it long on the condition that they wore it pinned back in tight braids.<ref name="Lost Stars">''[[Lost Stars]]''</ref> Beards were not common among [[Imperial Military|Imperial military]] personnel, and [[Thane Kyrell]] thus used beard suppressant during his time enlisted.<ref name="Lost Stars2" />

[[File:Kylo_and_Ren_argue.jpg|thumb|right|300px|The long, flowing hair of Supreme Leader Kylo Ren (left) was not to the military standards of General Armitage Hux (right).]]
The [[First Order]] also had regulations on hair length. [[General]] [[Armitage Hux]] secretly disapproved of [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren's]] hairstyle, which did not conform to the First Order's requirements. Convinced that an effective leader ruled by example, Hux felt that Ren's long hair was an "indignant assault" on his office as [[Supreme Leader]]. Hux's disapproval was such that he came to see it as a reminder of everything that he hated about Ren whom he saw lacking in discipline and military bearing. Hux vowed that if he replaced Ren as Supreme Leader, his first act would be to force his predecessor to "cut off his hair."<ref name="TROS EE">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: Expanded Edition]]''</ref>

===Practical uses===
The [[Nightsisters]] of [[Dathomir]] could inflict a [[Magick|curse]] on a given individual by creating a [[wax]]en effigy of that person. The creation of the effigy required a lock of the intended victim's hair.<ref name="M">{{TCW|Massacre}}</ref>

[[Gender|Female]] [[porg]]s crafted nests by using hair, fiber, or [[grass]].<ref name="The Best Pet">{{IDWAdventuresCite-2017|issue=5|story=Tales from Wild Space: The Best Pet}}</ref>

[[Range trooper]] [[Vambrace armor|armor]] had large pads of white [[synth-fur]], a synthetic form of hair, on its shoulders and lining the interior of its [[kama]] to keep the rugged troopers warm on cold-weather planets, such as [[Vandor]].<ref name="SoloOG">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story The Official Guide]]''</ref>

